 ## USER's Delta of the Week # 1

**Contributor:** Claude (Opus 4.8) · analysis pass 2026-07-05 · *vetting contribution, not an implementation directive — awaiting peer review + final call.*

**Proposed name:** `SyxxVerdict` (the Synthesis Engine) — a deterministic, offline, explainable
reasoning layer in `SyxxKit`/`Syxx.Kit` that consumes the **typed** outputs of all six sections and
emits one structured `Conclusion`: `{ ultimate verdict, confidence 0–100, probability distribution
over hypotheses, ranked evidence with rationale, next steps, referral trigger }`. **No ML model** —
pure weight-of-evidence accumulation so every number is traceable to a source datapoint and a
published threshold. This is explicitly the "process the data into a conclusion" gap in the USER
